S1 · Creating a server: new McpServer(serverInfo, options)
SDK: new McpServer(), client.getServerVersion(), client.getInstructions(), client.getServerCapabilities()
══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

── A. serverInfo only (name + version) ───────────────────────────────────────
   ℹ parameters: {"serverInfo":{"name":"demo-a","version":"1.0.0"}}

▶ What the client sees after connecting
  getServerVersion / getInstructions / getServerCapabilities()
  ✔ 0ms → 
    {
      "serverVersion": {
        "name": "demo-a",
        "version": "1.0.0"
      },
      "instructions": null,
      "capabilities": {},
      "protocolEra": "modern"
    }

── B. + title + instructions ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
   ℹ parameters: {"serverInfo":{"name":"demo-b","title":"Demo B","version":"1.1.0"},"options":{"instructions":"Call search_students before any other tool."}}

▶ What the client sees after connecting
  getServerVersion / getInstructions / getServerCapabilities()
  ✔ 0ms → 
    {
      "serverVersion": {
        "name": "demo-b",
        "title": "Demo B",
        "version": "1.1.0"
      },
      "instructions": "Call search_students before any other tool.",
      "capabilities": {},
      "protocolEra": "modern"
    }

── C. + capabilities.logging + one tool ──────────────────────────────────────
   ℹ parameters: {"serverInfo":{"name":"demo-c","version":"1.0.0"},"options":{"capabilities":{"logging":{}}},"tools":["echo"]}

▶ What the client sees after connecting
  getServerVersion / getInstructions / getServerCapabilities()
  ✔ 0ms → 
    {
      "serverVersion": {
        "name": "demo-c",
        "version": "1.0.0"
      },
      "instructions": null,
      "capabilities": {
        "logging": {},
        "tools": {
          "listChanged": true
        }
      },
      "protocolEra": "modern"
    }

── D. the real academic server (tools + resources + prompts + logging) ───────
   ℹ parameters: {"factory":"createAcademicServer"}

▶ What the client sees after connecting
  getServerVersion / getInstructions / getServerCapabilities()
  ✔ 0ms → 
    {
      "serverVersion": {
        "name": "academic",
        "title": "Academic Records",
        "version": "1.0.0"
      },
      "instructions": "Academic records server. Scores are on the 10-point scale; letter grades are A/B/C/D/F; GPA is on the 4-point scale. When the user gives a name instead of a student ID, call search_students first. Semesters look like \"2024-1\". Read academic://rules/grading for the exact grading rules.",
      "capabilities": {
        "logging": {},
        "completions": {},
        "prompts": {
          "listChanged": true
        },
        "resources": {
          "subscribe": true,
          "listChanged": true
        },
        "tools": {
          "listChanged": true
        }
      },
      "protocolEra": "modern"
    }

